  "other_facts": "Definitions: old IEM = >=30% ineffective liquid swallows; new IEM = >=50% ineffective liquid swallows. Group A (old IEM) N=150; Group B (new IEM, subset of A) N=101; Group C (patients who did not retain new definition) N=49. IEM classified as mild (normal bolus transit for both liquid and viscous), moderate (abnormal bolus transit for either), severe (abnormal bolus transit for both). No statistical difference in frequency of mild, moderate, or severe IEM between group A and B. Group C had significantly higher frequency of mild IEM and significantly lower frequency of severe IEM than group B. Heartburn: group B 25.7% vs group C 10.2%, P=0.03. Dysphagia: group B 24.8% vs group C 12.3%, P=0.08 (trend).",
  "summary": "The study indicates that IEM with >=50% ineffective liquid swallows (new definition) is frequently associated with bolus transit abnormalities and esophageal symptoms."
}

