  "other_facts": "Bleeding is the leading cause of preventable death in trauma, and early identification of hemorrhage improves outcomes. Current triage tools use transfusion receipt as a surrogate outcome and may misclassify patients who receive prompt hemorrhage control procedure without transfusion, die before transfusion, or receive unnecessary transfusion. Actionable hemorrhage was defined within 6 hours of emergency department arrival as actual or estimated pretransfusion hemoglobin <8 g/dL, performance of a hemorrhage control procedure irrespective of transfusion receipt, or death within 24 hours with autopsy supporting bleeding as the cause of death. The cohort was treated at three level 1 pediatric trauma centers between 2019 and 2021. Level of evidence was Diagnostic Test and Criteria, Level III.",
