  "safety": [],
  "other_facts": "Mestranol is a widely used estrogen converted into its active metabolite ethinyl estradiol by cytochrome P450 (CYP) 2C9. Wild-type CYP2C9*1 and 35 allelic variants were highly expressed in Sf21 insect cell microsomes. Incubation was performed at 37°C. Metabolite production was analyzed using high-performance liquid chromatography (HPLC). Atypical kinetics in 9 variants were largely due to a self-inhibitory effect in response to mestranol. This is the first report of these rare alleles for mestranol metabolism, providing fundamental data for further clinical studies.",
  "summary": "This in vitro study characterized the enzymatic activity of 36 CYP2C9 variants from Chinese individuals in metabolizing mestranol, revealing that most variants have decreased clearance and nine exhibit atypical kinetics due to self-inhibition."
}

