  "other_facts": "Post-donation symptoms may include fatigue, dizziness, or headache and could influence donor retention. Linear mixed models were used to determine change in symptoms for male and female donors separately. Multivariable regression was used to investigate associations with physical characteristics and donor return. Age, BMI, blood pressure in male donors, and blood volume in female donors were significantly associated with post-donation symptoms. Post-symptoms improve up to 3 days after whole blood donation. Results may help blood collection centers identify donors more prone to post-donation symptoms and provide personalized information about the presence and course of post-donation symptoms, possibly increasing donor return rates.",
  "summary": "In 3,076 whole blood donors in The Netherlands, post-donation symptoms such as fatigue were common but generally improved by day 3, with fatigue associated with donor characteristics and subsequent donor return."
}

