      "event": "CFU persistence (inhalation, Bt kurstaki)",
      "rate": "1/10"
    }
  ],
  "other_facts": "Intratracheal instillation and inhalation studies were performed. Two commercial biopesticides based on Bt subspecies kurstaki and israelensis. Control mice instilled with sterile water. Plethysmography showed no airway irritation. 70 days after exposure, half of instilled mice had remaining CFU. 3 out of 17 mice had interstitial lung inflammation after inhalation. 1 out of 10 mice had CFU after kurstaki inhalation.",
  "summary": "Repeated low dose aerosol exposures to commercial Bt based biopesticides can induce sub-chronic lung inflammation in mice, which may be the first step in development of chronic lung diseases, and inhalation of Bt aerosols does not induce airway irritation."
}

