  "other_facts": "No single UA parameter had both high sensitivity and high specificity. Absence of leukocyte esterase and pyuria had a high NPV for significant bacteriuria. Combined UA parameters did not perform better than pyuria alone with regard to NPV. High NPV of pyuria was maintained among most patient subgroups except females aged ≥65 years and patients with indwelling catheters. 18 different UA criteria were combined and 5 best-performing models were identified using receiver operating curves. Reflex urine culture algorithms, clinical decision support, and education targeting symptomatic patients are recommended.",
  "summary": "This retrospective cohort study of 221,933 encounters found that no single urinalysis parameter had both high sensitivity and specificity for predicting significant bacteriuria, but absence of pyuria had a high negative predictive value (≥0.90) except in females aged ≥65 and patients with indwelling catheters."
}

