  "other_facts": "Study name: VALIGA, designed to validate the Oxford Classification of IgAN. Renal biopsies scored for MEST score (M1, E1, S1, T1-2) and crescents (C1). Progression also assessed as rate of renal function decline (slope of eGFR). Statistical methods used: Cox regression and tree classification binary models. Cox analysis failed to prove predictive value of MEST M, S, and T scores in the sub-group of 174 children aged <18 years. Risk factors in subjects with M0: initial proteinuria >=0.4 g/day/1.73 m2 and eGFR <90 ml/min/1.73 m2. Children aged <16 years with M0 and well-preserved eGFR (>90 ml/min/1.73 m2) had a higher remission rate following treatment with corticosteroid and/or immunosuppressive therapy.",
  "summary": "This validation study of 261 young patients with IgAN identified clinical and histological risk factors associated with disease progression using Cox regression and tree classification models."
}

