  "summary": "A lamotrigine-loaded buccal micellar film (LTG-BF1) demonstrated superior antiepileptic efficacy in a PTZ-induced acute epileptic rat model compared to an oral market product, with reduced seizure scores, longer latency, higher threshold, and modulation of brain biomarkers."
