  "other_facts": "Heparin is a widely applied anticoagulant, and quantification of heparin concentration is pivotal for clinical use. Amino-group-modified silicon nanoparticles and glutathione-capped gold nanoclusters self-assemble into spherical particle structures via electrostatic interaction, resulting in aggregation-enhanced emission of GSH-AuNCs. Heparin is a highly sulfated glycosaminoglycan with much more negative charges, can bind silicon nanoparticles, and inhibits aggregation, causing aggregation-enhanced emission quenching of GSH-AuNCs while silicon nanoparticles retain their blue fluorescence. Silicon nanoparticles act as an internal reference, and GSH-AuNCs are used as a signal probe.",
