  "summary": "Prospective genomic profiling of 459 adult IDH-wildtype glioblastomas identified a distinct subgroup (2%) with replication repair deficiency, Lynch syndrome, and hypermutation, associated with younger age, giant cell histology, unique molecular profile, and prolonged median overall survival of 36.8 months, with promising response to immune checkpoint blockade."
