  },
  "outcomes": [
    {
      "measure": "offset of antiplatelet effect (PRU)",
      "timepoint": null,
      "effect": "10-24 hours",
      "ci": null
    }
  ],
  "safety": [],
  "other_facts": "Ticagrelor is contraindicated in combination with cytochrome P450 3A4 and 3A5 enzyme (CYP3A4/5) inducers due to increased clearance, causing diminished antiplatelet effects. The emergent nature of acute coronary syndromes (ACS) may preclude scrutinization of home medications before P2Y12 inhibitor administration. The purpose of this case series is to establish the temporal impact of CYP3A4/5 enzyme induction on ticagrelor's pharmacodynamic effect by utilizing VerifyNow platelet aggregation studies. Anticipated offset of antiplatelet effect is 36-48 hours. This was consistent across CYP3A4/5-inducing medications including carbamazepine, phenobarbital, and phenytoin. Monitoring of PRU every 6-12 hours with subsequent loading with clopidogrel or prasugrel should be considered. Larger scale studies are warranted to confirm these results.",
  "summary": "This retrospective case series of three patients demonstrates that CYP3A4/5 enzyme induction dramatically shortens the antiplatelet effect of ticagrelor in acute coronary syndromes."
}

