  "other_facts": "Resistant hypertension defined as uncontrolled blood pressure despite using three antihypertensive agents including a diuretic or need of four or more drugs. No significant difference between groups in age, sex, smoking, or body mass index. Office and ambulatory blood pressures and mean number of antihypertensive drugs used were significantly higher in RH patients. Plasma neurotensin levels: RH median 0.380 ng/ml (IQR 0.292-0.471); CH median 0.638 ng/ml (IQR 0.483-0.783). Multivariate analysis showed neurotensin is an independent predictor for resistant hypertension. Optimal cut-off value of neurotensin for RH was <0.509 ng/ml. Study is the first to show a correlation between lower neurotensin levels and RH. Recruitment was prospective.",
