    "duration": null
  },
  "outcomes": [
    {
      "measure": "mean weekly warfarin dose (nystatin group)",
      "timepoint": "after antifungal drugs",
      "effect": "9 mg",
      "ci": null
    },
    {
      "measure": "mean INR (nystatin group)",
      "timepoint": "after antifungal drugs",
      "effect": "10.6",
      "ci": null
    },
    {
      "measure": "mean weekly warfarin dose (miconazole oral gel group)",
      "timepoint": "after antifungal drugs",
      "effect": "10.8 mg",
      "ci": null
    },
    {
      "measure": "mean INR (miconazole oral gel group)",
      "timepoint": "after antifungal drugs",
      "effect": "8.8",
      "ci": null
    }
  ],
  "safety": [
    {
      "event": "bleeding complications (overall)",
      "rate": "44.2% (19/43)"
    },
    {
      "event": "bleeding complications (miconazole oral gel)",
      "rate": "15/32"
    },
    {
      "event": "bleeding complications (nystatin solution)",
      "rate": "4/8"
    }
  ],
  "other_facts": "Medline search disclosed 10 case reports of interactions between oral anticoagulants and miconazole oral gel, but none so far between nystatin solution and anticoagulants. Miconazole oral gel was prescribed for 32 patients, nystatin solution for eight patients and miconazole vaginal suppositories for three patients. Before use of the antifungal drugs, the mean weekly warfarin dose in the nystatin group was 14.5 mg (P = 0.038) and mean INR was 2.5 (range 1.9-3.5). After antifungal drugs in nystatin group, INR was 10.6 (range 4.5-19.3, P = 0.0001). In the miconazole oral gel group, mean weekly warfarin dose before was 15.7 mg (P = 0.008) and mean INR before was 2.44 (range 1.92-3.18). After antifungal drugs in miconazole oral gel group, INR was 8.8 (range 4.9-16.9, P < 0.0001). Miconazole oral gel and topically applied nystatin solution have equally strong effects on warfarin activity and can provoke major bleeding. Prospective evaluation of this effect is called for. Warfarin dose adjustment appears necessary when the anticoagulant is used concomitantly with those topical antifungals.",
  "summary": "A retrospective study of 43 patients on stable anticoagulation found that miconazole oral gel and topically applied nystatin solution have equally strong effects on warfarin activity, significantly increasing INR and provoking major bleeding in 44.2% of patients."
}

