  "other_facts": "Primary endpoint was to demonstrate a 40% rate of 6-month progression-free survival; the study did not achieve this endpoint. Motexafin gadolinium disrupts redox-dependent pathways by inhibiting oxidative stress-related proteins, leading to apoptosis; it selectively targets tumor cells, disrupting energy metabolism and repair mechanisms, rendering cells more prone to apoptosis. Preclinical studies with motexafin gadolinium and pemetrexed showed significant tumor growth delay in lung cancer cell lines. The combination was well tolerated, with toxicity similar to pemetrexed alone. Response rate, progression-free survival, and overall survival did not seem markedly different from prior phase II and phase III studies of pemetrexed alone. There are no further plans for development of this combination.",
