  "summary": "In patients with septic shock requiring prehospital mobile ICU intervention, prehospital blood lactate clearance <10% was associated with increased 30-day mortality (HRa 2.04, 95% CI 1.08-3.84), while clearance >10% was protective (HRa 0.49, 95% CI 0.26-0.92)."
}
