  "safety": null,
  "other_facts": "In vitro cell lines used: ER-positive (MCF-7 and T47D) and ER-negative (MDA-MB-231 and Hs 578T) human breast cancer cells. In vitro deprenyl concentrations: 10(-3) to 10(-8) M. Saline-treated tumor-bearing rats exhibited reduced splenic NA innervation, NE content, IL-2, IFN-γ, NK cell activity, and DLN IL-2 and IFN-γ levels compared to young female rats without tumors. Conclusions: Development of mammary tumors is mediated through loss of immunity and sympathetic NA nerve fibers accompanied by reduced NE levels in the spleen. Prevention by deprenyl may involve reversal of tumor-associated decline in sympathetic NA activity and cell-mediated immune responses in the spleen and DLN. Antitumor effects of deprenyl may be partially mediated through ER-dependent intracellular signaling pathways.",
  "summary": "L-deprenyl treatment in early middle-aged female rats prevented spontaneous mammary tumor development, enhanced sympathetic noradrenergic innervation and cell-mediated immune responses, and partly inhibited ER-positive breast cancer cell proliferation in vitro."
}

