  "other_facts": "Enrollment occurred between October 1998 and October 2004. Morphine hydrochloride solution (0.2 mg/ml) was prepared without preservatives under a flow laminar air box (class 100). Maternal age and opiate dose during pregnancy were assessed, but values were not reported. Neonatal gestational age at delivery, birth weight, Lipsitz scores, daily morphine dose, maximum morphine dose, duration of NAS, and duration of treatment required to achieve stable Lipsitz scores below 4 were outcome measures; numerical values for gestational age, birth weight, maximum morphine dose, and duration of NAS were not reported. Kruskal-Wallis test was used for comparison of median values. Doses could be adjusted with a margin of 0.02 mg. Because delayed onset of NAS may occur up to 7 days, infants born to mothers treated with buprenorphine should be kept in the hospital for an appropriate surveillance period. The hospital morphine solution was concluded to be adequate for management of NAS.",
